class:: TemporalDecrease
summary:: Relative downward slope of a rolling RMS envelope
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Amplitude

description::
Fits a straight line to RMS amplitude versus seconds, negates the slope, and divides by mean RMS amplitude. Positive output means overall decay and negative output means growth. This MIRa definition is a dimensionless relative change per second, not spectral decrease.

Frames contain nonoverlapping RMS measurements. Output stays zero until a complete observation window is available, then updates once per RMS frame. Silence returns zero. Runtime cost is linear in windowTime/frameTime per update; there is no callback allocation. These descriptors are rolling summaries and do not segment individual events. Formulas are independently implemented from standard weighted moments and linear regression.

The nearest vanilla building block is link::Classes/Amplitude::, which tracks instantaneous level; this UGen summarizes its recent distribution in time.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: floorDB
Silence floor in dBFS, clipped to -160..0. Used by dynamic complexity and dB regression; temporal moments use the original energy.

returns::
Signed relative decrease per second.

examples::
TemporalDecrease fits a linear regression line to RMS envelope values versus time, negating the slope and normalizing by mean RMS amplitude. Positive values signify natural decay over the observation window; negative values signify envelope growth. In this example, temporal decrease controls an upward dynamic expander to smoothly linearize and sustain natural instrument note ring-downs. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time temporal decrease slope.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("plucks.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic pluck fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
            var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.4), trig);
            Pluck.ar(WhiteNoise.ar * env, trig, 0.2, 1/220, 2.0, 0.3)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var decrease = TemporalDecrease.kr(source, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var decLag = decrease.lag(0.08);
        var sustainBoost = decLag.linlin(0, 6, 1.0, 2.5).clip(1.0, 3.0);
        var expanded = (source * sustainBoost).softclip * 0.25;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, decLag.clip(-5, 10)) };
        expanded * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Temporal Decrease", ~miraBus, -2.0, 8.0, "slope");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
